# Line endings are part of the contract: byte caps (T11 SKILL.md ≤49000B),
# content checks and `bash -n` are all byte-sensitive — windows autocrlf
# otherwise mangles checkouts (windows-latest CI saw SKILL.md 49732B vs
# 48967B = +1 CR per line, and every .sh unparseable). Force LF everywhere;
# batch files keep CRLF (cmd.exe goto/label semantics).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.webm binary
*.wav binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
